1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,070
Good morning,

2
00:00:01,070 --> 00:00:04,080
and welcome to City Football Club.

3
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:09,859
I’d like to give you some useful information about your visit to the stadium

4
00:00:09,859 --> 00:00:10,682
today,

5
00:00:10,682 --> 00:00:14,736
and then we’ll start the tour of the areas of the stadium that are

6
00:00:14,736 --> 00:00:15,940
open to visitors.

7
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:18,751
I can see lots of children here today,

8
00:00:18,751 --> 00:00:23,690
so just to let mums and dads know a few things before we start.

9
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:26,084
The stadium has lots of stairs,

10
00:00:26,084 --> 00:00:28,900
and the players’ tunnel is very dark.

11
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:33,961
Please don’t let your children wander off on their own, even for a

12
00:00:33,961 --> 00:00:34,780
minute.

13
00:00:34,780 --> 00:00:38,700
We don’t want any accidents or anyone getting frightened.

14
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:40,644
Cameras are permitted everywhere,

15
00:00:40,644 --> 00:00:45,990
and you can take pictures of your child shooting a penalty.

16
00:00:45,990 --> 00:00:48,323
Assistants are helping to organise this,

17
00:00:48,323 --> 00:00:53,378
and hopefully the queue won’t be too long – it’s very hot

18
00:00:53,378 --> 00:00:56,100
and sunny out on the pitch today.

19
00:00:56,100 --> 00:01:00,117
You can get food and drink at the café,

20
00:01:00,117 --> 00:01:04,580
and I really recommend the healthy lunch boxes for children.

21
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:11,410
Also in the café, children are invited to do a football-themed drawing.

22
00:01:11,410 --> 00:01:15,896
We’ll pick the best one at the end of the afternoon,

23
00:01:15,896 --> 00:01:21,130
so don’t forget to put your name and contact details on the back.

24
00:01:21,130 --> 00:01:26,654
That way, if you’ve left the stadium before then, we’ll send your

25
00:01:26,654 --> 00:01:27,048
prize,

26
00:01:27,048 --> 00:01:29,810
but sadly we can’t return drawings.

27
00:01:29,810 --> 00:01:34,280
I’d like to mention some features of the tour.

28
00:01:34,280 --> 00:01:37,863
We’ll start with the three-sixty cinema experience,

29
00:01:37,863 --> 00:01:41,445
which has been very popular over the years,

30
00:01:41,445 --> 00:01:49,506
and then I’ll take you to the players’ dressing rooms before going outside to the seating area

31
00:01:49,506 --> 00:01:50,850
and the pitch.

32
00:01:50,850 --> 00:01:59,194
I should say, if you’d prefer your visit to be self-guided, please collect headphones from the reception

33
00:01:59,194 --> 00:02:05,220
and then you can listen to the pre-recorded information at your own speed.

34
00:02:05,220 --> 00:02:08,697
We’ve only just introduced this feature,

35
00:02:08,697 --> 00:02:11,180
and would appreciate your feedback.

36
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:15,690
We’re thinking of offering tours in other languages in future

37
00:02:15,690 --> 00:02:21,020
so if you have any thoughts on that, we’d welcome those too.

38
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:27,026
If you plan to return another time, you might like to book one of

39
00:02:27,026 --> 00:02:31,316
our VIP tours – we’ve only just started offering these,

40
00:02:31,316 --> 00:02:33,890
and they can be booked online.

41
00:02:33,890 --> 00:02:41,121
Now, the stadium you see today was built in 1989, as part of a

42
00:02:41,121 --> 00:02:42,670
three-year redevelopment project

43
00:02:42,670 --> 00:02:48,865
while that project was going on, the team had to play its matches at

44
00:02:48,865 --> 00:02:54,617
the ground of another club – apart from that, the club has been here

45
00:02:54,617 --> 00:02:56,830
on this site since 1870.

46
00:02:56,830 --> 00:02:59,246
As some of you may know,

47
00:02:59,246 --> 00:03:04,882
that was the start of a really important decade in the history of football

48
00:03:04,882 --> 00:03:06,090
in this country.

49
00:03:06,090 --> 00:03:12,408
For example, 1870 was also the year that football teams started to include a

50
00:03:12,408 --> 00:03:16,470
player whose role it was to guard the goal.

51
00:03:16,470 --> 00:03:22,710
It’s hard to imagine what the game must have been like without someone in

52
00:03:22,710 --> 00:03:24,790
that position, isn’t it?

53
00:03:24,790 --> 00:03:32,246
In 1872 and 73, many other clubs were established, both here and abroad,

54
00:03:32,246 --> 00:03:40,276
and the following year, in 1874, referees were allowed to send players off if

55
00:03:40,276 --> 00:03:42,570
they committed certain offences.

56
00:03:42,570 --> 00:03:49,340
And also in that year, teams started having to swap ends at half-time.

57
00:03:49,340 --> 00:03:55,192
One fact I was interested to discover was that in early football games, the

58
00:03:55,192 --> 00:04:00,626
aim was for the scorer to get the ball between two flag posts,

59
00:04:00,626 --> 00:04:06,060
and later between sticks joined at the top with a piece of tape.

60
00:04:06,060 --> 00:04:07,186
In 1875,

61
00:04:07,186 --> 00:04:15,070
that tape was replaced with the solid crossbar that we’re familiar with today.

62
00:04:15,070 --> 00:04:18,660
1877 saw the founding of further new clubs,

63
00:04:18,660 --> 00:04:24,943
and the history books tell us that in the same year, all the clubs

64
00:04:24,943 --> 00:04:29,880
decided to set a limit of ninety minutes for each match.

65
00:04:29,880 --> 00:04:33,502
Before that, it was a more casual arrangement,

66
00:04:33,502 --> 00:04:38,483
and this sometimes caused huge arguments – and sometimes fights – during matches,

67
00:04:38,483 --> 00:04:47,086
when one team called the end of the game and the other team wanted to play on to try

68
00:04:47,086 --> 00:04:49,350
and score a winning goal.

69
00:04:49,350 --> 00:04:56,290
By 1878, the number of teams in the football league increased again.

70
00:04:56,290 --> 00:04:59,856
In addition, referees started using whistles,

71
00:04:59,856 --> 00:05:04,610
and electric lamps were installed on certain pitches.

72
00:05:04,610 --> 00:05:11,511
This was a significant change, as games could then be played in the evenings

73
00:05:11,511 --> 00:05:12,990
all year round.

74
00:05:12,990 --> 00:05:21,745
In 1880, clubs began to charge fans for admission to games, even though players were still amateurs

75
00:05:21,745 --> 00:05:24,320
and had other ‘proper’ jobs.

76
00:05:24,320 --> 00:05:31,139
That’s hard to imagine in the modern professional game where top players earn significant

77
00:05:31,139 --> 00:05:35,230
sums of money from both playing and commercial activities.
